cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Harmonia in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Harmonia: local-first music analysis and harmonic mixing assistance"
abstract: >-
  Harmonia analyses a local music library with digital signal processing,
  computing tempo, musical key, energy and danceability, and recommends
  harmonically compatible tracks using the Camelot wheel. Key detection is
  benchmarked against the GiantSteps+ EDM Key dataset with MIREX weighting;
  the remaining descriptors are documented heuristics with no ground truth.
  Harmonia began as a third-year LEI capstone project at the Instituto
  Superior de Engenharia do Porto (ISEP), supervised by Prof. Carlos Ferreira,
  and has since been rebuilt as a locally deployable open-source tool.
